All written by moist-mason, hence the use of first person.

CURRENT [0.4.0]
- Logging
	- Ensure that most exceptions call the AcpException class, so that they appear in logs if something arises.
- Testing
	- Fix mod injection in legacy modded test. Low priority because the code for mod stuff *should* work still.
- General
	- Figure out how to fix the dependency resolving messages from showing in logs, even if the dependencies are actually resolved.
		- UPDATE 12/15: Dependency resolution needs to happen, so any condition that prevents the ResolveLibraries or ResolveTools steps will make
		Java processes fail. I will continue to find a workaround but this may actually be a necessary evil.
	- Figure out how to resolve the resolution problems that cause the game's display to not fit the entire window. This is 100% something that
	occurred once ACP was updated from Java 8 to Java 21.

FUTURE [1.0]
- Likely rework of the ModLoader download system. Instead of LZMA I am considering using a DiffPatch system, which is
what NeoForge uses. This will allow the ModLoader text to be more readable, and will be especially important as future versions of Minecraft,
which rely on Forge, become supported by ACP.
- Refactoring of older code that I haven't really touched in a while, like the classes for archive creation. I also
want to take a look at the RepackageDefault and MakeReobfSrg classes, as I've honestly forgotten what those are for. I believe the RepackageDefault
will not be used anymore if the ModLoader rework is achieved. MakeReobfSrg might still be.